; Generated by tools/gen_installer_voices.py -- do not edit by hand.
;
; The languages and voices the installer offers, the rule files each
; language needs, and installed.ini -- the record of what was chosen,
; which the catalogue reads back so that Windows is told about those
; voices and no others. Included by Infovox230SAPI.iss.
;
; 60 voices in 12 languages.

[Components]
; A language carries its own rule files, so the size shown against it on
; the components page is the real cost of adding it. The voices inside it
; cost nothing but a name in the Windows voice list: the five speakers of
; a language differ only in four numbers and all five read the same file.
;
; Each voice is named in full rather than just "Male": on that page a
; screen reader reads the line it is on and not the branch above it, and
; "Male" on its own does not say which language it belongs to.

; American English -- AMRULES.IVX, 2.4 MB
Name: "am"; Description: "American English"; Types: full english minimal
Name: "am\male"; Description: "American English Male"; Types: full english minimal
Name: "am\female"; Description: "American English Female"; Types: full english minimal
Name: "am\child"; Description: "American English Child"; Types: full english
Name: "am\giant"; Description: "American English Giant"; Types: full english
Name: "am\zombie"; Description: "American English Zombie"; Types: full english

